==Strategy==
This stage introduces Deathshund, who unlike the original Dagshund, trades his rapid attacks for really high range and crushing damage per hit, similar to a Le'boin variant. In addition, Deathshund's burrow and his high health means that if you don't Z-Kill him he can quickly take up your time. Trying to Z-Kill him without the usage of Ubers or [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Island Cat]] is also a pain given that even [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Awakened Musashi]] gets outranged by him. Because of this, your cannon should be the [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] to make sure he can't do too much damage to your units.

Aside from Mr. Bony Bone himself, this is a relatively simple Ostromeda fight with Deathshund, a single Zang Roo, as well as Prof. Owlbrowley. The startoff of the stage is no joke, having a Zang Roo that spawns before your Holy Blast is ready, meaning you need to be careful about how much room it takes up.

After you hit the base, lure Ostromeda and his companions to your base, where your goal is to simply just beat him up. While there is another Zang Roo on base hit, do not Holy Blast it as using your Holy Blast for the burrowing Deathshund is much more important. Aside from that, this is a relatively simple Ostromeda fight, with [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] serving as your main way to damage Owlbrowley and everyone else while a meatshield of your choice and [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] helps to stall everyone. The Zombie threats should die relatively fast with [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], while for Ostromeda himself just remember to bring methods of CC  like [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] or [[Master of Life Dr. Nova (Special Cat)|Nova]] and strong damaging options like a Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] or [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]].

